# Build output
# COMMITTED build artifacts (the "fork & go" ethos — shipped, not ignored):
#   index.html + assets/ — the Vite bundle (codex.js/codex.css), promoted to the
#                          repo root by scripts/promote-build.mjs. This IS the app
#                          you run (node server.js / GitHub Pages). Source template
#                          is index.src.html. Rebuild: `npm run build`.
#   vendor/codex-llm.cjs — @codex/core/llm bundled to CJS for the Node server (scripts/build-server-llm.mjs)
# dist-web/ (below) is the intermediate Vite outDir — ignored; only the promoted
# root copy is committed.
build/
*.bundle.js

# Testing
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# Temporary
*.tmp
.cache/
.claude/

# BTC donation pool — server-side state, never commit
data/donations.json
data/donations.json.tmp
data/donations.audit.log

# Internal dev artifacts (architecture map + foundation plan — not for the public PWA)
_arch-viz.html
FOUNDATION.md
dist-web/

# Generated Vite entry — regenerated from index.src.html by scripts/gen-web-entry.mjs
# on every `npm run build`. Don't version the generated artifact.
index.vite.html

